NAME
       bal asyncapi ws - Generate Ballerina files from an AsyncAPI
                         definition for WebSocket protocol, or
                         generate an AsyncAPI definition from a
                         Ballerina service file

SYNOPSIS
       bal asyncapi ws -i <asyncapi-definition-file-path>
                       [-o <output-directory>]
                       [--license <license-file-path>]
                       [--json]
                       [--service <service-name>]
                       [--with-tests]

DESCRIPTION
       Generates Ballerina source files from an AsyncAPI definition
       file for WebSocket protocol integrations.

       When --service is provided, the direction is reversed: the
       command reads a Ballerina service file given by --input and
       generates an AsyncAPI definition for the named service.
       In this mode, --json controls whether the output definition
       is written as JSON instead of the default YAML.

       The --input flag is mandatory in both modes.

OPTIONS
        -i, --input <asyncapi-definition-file-path>
                This is a mandatory input. The path to the AsyncAPI
                definition file (.yaml, .yml, or .json) for
                spec-to-code generation, or the path to the
                Ballerina service file (.bal) for code-to-spec
                generation.

        -o, --output <output-directory>
                This is an optional input. The path to the target
                output directory for the generated files.
                The default is the current working directory.

        --license <license-file-path>
                This is an optional input. The path to a file
                containing the license header to be added to all
                generated Ballerina files.

        --json
                This is an optional input. If set, the generated
                AsyncAPI definition is written in JSON format
                instead of the default YAML format. Applicable
                only in code-to-spec mode (when --service is used).

        --service <service-name>
                This is an optional input. The name of the service
                in the Ballerina source file for which an AsyncAPI
                definition should be generated. When this flag is
                provided the tool switches to code-to-spec mode.

        --with-tests
                This is an optional input. If set, test files are
                generated alongside the service files. Applicable
                only in spec-to-code mode.

        -h, --help
                Display help for the ws subcommand.

EXAMPLES
       Generate Ballerina WebSocket files from an AsyncAPI definition.
           $ bal asyncapi ws -i definition.yaml

       Generate Ballerina WebSocket files into a specific output
       directory and also generate test files.
           $ bal asyncapi ws -i definition.yaml \
                             -o ./generated \
                             --with-tests

       Generate an AsyncAPI definition from a Ballerina service file.
           $ bal asyncapi ws -i service.bal --service ChatService
